  "goodToKnow": "Das Schlachtfeld is a battlefield: auf dem Schlachtfeld fallen. Famous German battlefields include the Teutoburg Forest (9 AD, where Germanic tribes defeated Roman legions) and Leipzig (Völkerschlacht, 1813, with its huge monument). Humorously, a messy room sieht aus wie ein Schlachtfeld. Die Schlacht is a battle, and schlachten means to slaughter animals. Plural: die Schlachtfelder."
